# Portfolio Design Rules

## Follow the designs exactly
- Always implement what the user describes and shows in their Figma designs — do not deviate.
- If something the user asks for is not working, keep iterating until it works exactly as requested. Do not give up or offer workarounds.

## Layout: horizontal project gallery
- Home presents a project immediately (after the KATARINA load-in). No vertical card stack, no film-reel stages.
- Projects sit in a sideways rail. Native CSS `scroll-snap-type: x mandatory` with `snap-stop: always`. One gesture lands on the next project.
- Convert vertical wheel to horizontal scroll on the rail. Do not skip projects.
- Bottom-right menu: Home, About me, Resume. Bottom-center: scroll view and list view toggles.
- Name mark types in centered, then settles as the top-left logo.

## Reference
- Figma: project-first horizontal layout, Meshed Display titles, cyan KATA|RINA mark.
- Do not revive stacked peeking cards, wheel-lock animation, or glass card decks.
